            // FAQ Section
            'faq-label': 'Frequently Asked Questions',
            'faq-title-1': 'Common Inquiries About',
            'faq-title-2': 'RAZ Download Manager',
            'faq-desc': 'Transparent answers about how RAZ Download Manager works, its speed, and its open-source values.',
            'faq-q1': 'Is RAZ Download Manager truly 100% free forever?',
            'faq-a1': 'Yes, completely 100% free! RAZ Download Manager is licensed under the open-source GNU General Public License v3 (GPL-3.0). There are no paid tiers, no monthly subscriptions, no 30-day trial limitations, and no advertisements whatsoever.',
            'faq-q2': 'Why is it 5.4× faster than IDM in benchmarks?',
            'faq-a2': 'RAZ Download Manager is written from scratch in native Rust, providing near-instant socket initialization and zero runtime garbage collection pauses. It connects all parallel segments at once from millisecond zero and dynamically re-splits slow streams.',
            'faq-q3': 'Is it safe from malware, spyware, and adware?',
            'faq-a3': 'Completely safe. The entire source code is public and open for review on GitHub. Releases are compiled automatically by GitHub Actions CI/CD directly from the public repository. Every binary is published with cryptographic SHA-256 checksums.',
            'faq-q4': 'Can I download Torrents without third-party software?',
            'faq-a4': 'Yes! RAZ Download Manager includes a native BitTorrent client engine powered by librqbit. Simply click a magnet link or open a .torrent file to download selective files and watch the swarm pieces live.',
            'faq-q5': 'How do I install the browser extension?',
            'faq-a5': 'When running the setup installer, ensure browser integration is checked. For Chrome, Edge, Brave, and Opera, install it from the Chrome Web Store. For Firefox, grab it from Mozilla Add-ons. Links are provided on this page.',
            'faq-q6': 'Can I import my existing downloads from IDM?',
            'faq-a6': 'Yes. In IDM, go to Tasks → Export → To IDM export file. Then in RAZ Download Manager, select Tasks → Import → From IDM export file. Your links, queues, and progress will be imported seamlessly.',

